# Execution targets

Optional sealed-packet field `execution_target` (not one of the required seven).
Tokens: `worktree` (omitted/empty default; `.worktrees/<packet-id>`),
`isolated_copy`, `openshell:<name>`, `cloud_subagent`. Unknown tokens fail
closed — not coerced.

`openshell:<name>` matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,62}$`. Reserved names `hermes`,
`pi`, `eval` are illegal as the name and as `program.site_path`. Never
`openshell sandbox connect --editor cursor`. Never put app source in those
reserved sandboxes.

site-specialist defaults to `worktree`. operations-excellence `independent_review`
requires `isolated_copy` (oracle tree ≠ implementer tree) and does not follow
into OpenShell or `cloud_subagent`.

Ceilings: `max_depth=1`, `max_children=6`, `no_redelegation=true`. A green
sandbox/VM/worktree is not a named-gate PASS. Oracles remain
`scripts/harness/{verify,adversarial}.sh`. Agents never `--actor user`.
